{% set local_problem %}
<p>Scottsboro has two distinct housing situations, and both have gutter challenges.</p>

<p>Near Lake Guntersville, elevated humidity puts constant stress on gutter systems. The seams in sectional gutters — held together by caulk and crimped connections — degrade faster in this environment. We see 15-year-old sectional gutters near the lake that look worse than 25-year-old systems in drier areas. For lakeside homes (especially vacation properties that sit unattended), seamless gutters are a smarter long-term investment.</p>

<p>In town, many of Scottsboro's older homes still have original gutters from the 60s, 70s, or 80s. These systems have often been patched and repatched until they're more caulk than gutter. Replacing them with seamless gutters improves function and appearance while eliminating the constant maintenance headache.</p>

<p>Whether you're protecting a lakeside investment or updating a classic Scottsboro home, seamless gutters provide the leak-free, low-maintenance performance you need.</p>
{% endset %}

{% set service_explanation %}
<p>Seamless gutters are exactly what they sound like: continuous gutters with no seams except at corners and downspout connections. Unlike traditional sectional gutters (made of pre-cut 10-foot sections joined together), seamless gutters are fabricated on-site from a single piece of aluminum coil — custom-cut to the exact length of each run on your home.</p>

<p>Why does this matter? Because seams are where gutters fail. Every joint is a potential leak point, a place for debris to catch, and a weak spot that degrades over time — especially in humid environments like Scottsboro's. Seamless gutters eliminate these problems entirely.</p>

<p>We bring our portable gutter machine directly to your Scottsboro home and fabricate your gutters in your driveway. What comes out is a precision-fit gutter system designed specifically for your roofline.</p>
{% endset %}

{% set why_us %}
<p>We've been installing seamless gutters in Jackson County for over two decades. We understand the lake effect humidity, the mix of historic and lakeside homes, and the unique needs of vacation property owners.</p>

<p>From our Huntsville headquarters, Scottsboro is about a 50-minute drive. We serve the area regularly and can typically schedule estimates within a few days of your call.</p>
{% endset %}
